2. How a Request Flows from User to Pod
Step-by-step flow:
1.	User → LoadBalancer
o	External load balancer receives the request.
2.	LoadBalancer → Ingress Controller
o	Forwarded to the ingress controller service (NodePort or ClusterIP).
3.	Ingress Controller → Service
o	Ingress controller checks Ingress rules (host/path) and forwards to the target service.
4.	Service → kube-proxy
o	Service IP is virtual.
o	kube-proxy uses iptables/IPVS rules to route to the correct pod(s).
5.	Pod receives request
o	Pod processes the request and sends the response back along the same path.
Key points:
•	Service does not forward traffic itself; it’s a virtual abstraction.
•	kube-proxy does not run pods; it only handles networking.
•	LoadBalancer does not know ingress rules; it simply forwards traffic.
